LicoUp release source: staged entry for the compiled lico-gateway executable.

The release stage places the binary built from
`cargo build --manifest-path crates/licoup-gateway/entry/Cargo.toml --bin lico-gateway`
at this path before `tools/scripts/client-release-package-index.mjs build` packages
this directory into the package payload. The package owns that program: the kernel
declares no gateway target and links no part of the runtime, so the crate beside
this directory is what builds the entry the manifest names. Until the release
stage runs, the file is the staged entry the committed package declares: the
manifest names a process runtime with no runtimeRef, the release declaration
declares a native executable entry, and the packaging tooling refuses an entry
whose name or first two bytes mark it as a script. Nothing in the repository
executes this file; it exists so the declared native entry is present and the
payload packages deterministically from a checkout.
